    <node id="CDC">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">(No description provided in the data)
Relationships:
  - Source: CDC
  - Target: CANCER TREATMENT
  - Description: CDC.gov/tobacco provides smoking cessation resources; quitting smoking/vaping is important for effective cancer treatment.
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support option to help people quit smoking or vaping, while the CDC’s website, CDC.gov/tobacco, is also listed as an online support resource for quitting tobacco. Together, they serve as accessible digital tools for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and assistance to those looking to stop using tobacco products.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, the CDC provides these resources through its dedicated website, CDC.gov/tobacco. Together, BeTobaccoFree.gov and the CDC serve as accessible online support options to help people quit smoking or vaping. Both entities are listed as credible sources of assistance for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and resources for those looking to stop using tobacco products.
  - Source: CDC
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) operates the online resource CDC.gov/tobacco, which serves as the agency's dedicated digital platform for tobacco cessation. As the CDC's official online tobacco cessation resource, CDC.gov/tobacco provides information and support to help individuals quit tobacco use, reflecting the CDC's broader public health mission to reduce tobacco-related disease and death. This platform is a key component of the CDC's efforts to offer accessible cessation guidance and resources to the public.
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: CDC.gov/tobacco is the official tobacco resource page of the CDC (Centers for Disease Control and Prevention). As a dedicated web resource maintained by the CDC, it is designed to provide reliable information and online support for individuals looking to quit smoking or vaping. The CDC is the organization responsible for and associated with this website, ensuring that the content and resources offered align with public health guidelines and evidence-based cessation strategies.</data>
