Relationships:
  - Source: STEM CELL RESCUE
  - Target: PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA
  - Description: Stem cell rescue may be used for primary CNS lymphoma after other treatments or relapse
  - Source: STEM CELL RESCUE
  - Target: LYMPHOMA
  - Description: Stem cell rescue is used when lymphoma comes back after earlier treatment or after other treatments
  - Source: STEM CELL RESCUE
  - Target: RELAPSE
  - Description: Stem cell rescue is a treatment approach used for lymphoma when the disease has returned after an initial course of therapy. Specifically, it is indicated in the context of a relapse, meaning the lymphoma has come back following earlier treatment. The procedure is employed after the relapse occurs, serving as a subsequent line of intervention. Thus, stem cell rescue is directly associated with managing recurrent lymphoma, with the goal of addressing the disease after prior treatment has failed to provide a lasting remission.</data>
