    <node id="NEUROPATHOLOGIST">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A specialist who examines biopsy tissue under a microscope, performs histologic and molecular testing, sends results back to the neurosurgeon, and provides information used by the treatment team.
Relationships:
  - Source: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: The neuropathologist examines the tissue sample obtained from a biopsy.
  - Source: NEUROSURGEON
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: The neuropathologist sends analysis results back to the neurosurgeon.
  - Source: OPEN BIOPSY
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: Tissue from an open biopsy is examined by the neuropathologist.
  - Source: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Target: LABORATORY
  - Description: The neuropathologist works in association with the laboratory to examine biopsy samples.
  - Source: HISTOLOGY
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: The neuropathologist performs histologic analysis when inspecting tissue under a microscope.
  - Source: LAB TESTING
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: The neuropathologist performs the laboratory analysis of biopsy tissue.
  - Source: STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: A stereotactic biopsy sample is sent to the laboratory where the neuropathologist analyzes it.
  - Source: MOLECULAR TESTING
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: The neuropathologist performs molecular testing on the biopsy sample.
  - Source: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Target: HOSPITAL
  - Description: A hospital may or may not have a neuropathologist available; if not, the biopsy can be sent to one.
  - Source: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Target: MEDICAL CENTER
  - Description: A medical center may or may not have a neuropathologist available; if not, the biopsy can be sent to one.
  - Source: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Target: TREATMENT TEAM
  - Description: Neuropathologist findings and diagnostic information help the treatment team plan treatment.</data>
