    <node id="HEAD AND NECK CANCER">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Head and neck cancer is a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck region, encompassing malignancies of the oral cavity, oropharynx, nasopharynx, larynx, hypopharynx, and nasal cavity/paranasal sinuses. This group includes mouth cancer, and its development is strongly associated with tobacco and alcohol use as key risk factors. The diagnosis and treatment of head and neck cancer can have wide-ranging effects on a patient's health and quality of life. Treatment may impact the jaw, teeth, and gums, as well as overall oral health. Beyond the oral cavity, it can also affect endocrine glands, hearing, nutrition, speech, swallowing, fertility, and overall performance status. Thus, head and neck cancer represents a complex set of diseases requiring comprehensive care that addresses both the tumor and the multiple functional systems that may be compromised by the disease and its management.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: THROAT CANCER
  - Target: HEAD AND NECK CANCER
  - Description: Throat cancer is a type of head and neck cancer.
  - Source: HEAD AND NECK CANCER
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: Throat cancer is included in the group of cancers arising in the head and neck area
  - Source: HEAD AND NECK CANCER
  - Target: LARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Description: Laryngeal cancer is a type of head and neck cancer, arising in the larynx/voice box
  - Source: HEAD AND NECK CANCER
  - Target: HYPOPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Description: Head and neck cancer can occur in the hypopharynx, so hypopharyngeal cancer is a type of head and neck cancer</data>
