    <node id="MOLECULAR TESTING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">MOLECULAR TESTING is a diagnostic approach that analyzes biological samples—typically obtained through biopsy—to identify key genetic and protein-based features of a tumor. It is also known as biomarker testing, as it examines DNA, genes, or proteins to detect specific molecular alterations. In the context of gliomas, molecular testing helps determine tumor type, growth rate, and other distinctive characteristics that are critical for accurate diagnosis and prognosis. Beyond gliomas, this testing method is widely used to guide cancer treatment by revealing the unique molecular profile of a patient’s tumor, enabling more personalized and targeted therapeutic decisions.
Relationships:
  - Source: MOLECULAR TESTING
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: Molecular testing is performed on a biopsy sample to identify tumor characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
