    <node id="NASOPHARYNGEAL CANCER">
      <data key="d3">12</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Nasopharyngeal cancer (NPC), also known as nasopharyngeal carcinoma, is a type of head and neck cancer that arises in the nasopharynx—the upper part of the throat behind the nose, near the nasal cavity. It is considered a rare cancer overall, but it occurs most frequently in people from parts of Asia, Native America, and North Africa. The most common form of NPC is squamous cell carcinoma. Patient information for nasopharyngeal cancer is available through the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN).
**Relationships:**
  - Source: NASOPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: Nasopharyngeal cancer affects the nasopharynx, an upper part of the throat, so it is a type of throat cancer
  - Source: NASOPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Target: LARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Description: Nasopharyngeal cancer should not be confused with laryngeal cancer, another type of cancer affecting the throat
  - Source: NASOPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Target: HYPOPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Description: Nasopharyngeal cancer and hypopharyngeal cancer are cancers of different parts of the pharynx</data>
