  - Description: Advanced-stage prostate cancer is defined by metastasis, meaning the cancer has spread beyond the prostate to other parts of the body. This condition is characterized by the movement of cancerous cells from the prostate gland to distant sites, such as bones, lymph nodes, or other organs. In the context of this disease, metastasis is the key feature that distinguishes advanced-stage prostate cancer from localized prostate cancer, which remains confined within the prostate. Thus, advanced-stage prostate cancer and metastasis are closely linked, with the latter serving as the defining criterion for the former.
