    <node id="MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A test performed on a biopsy sample to examine molecular components and determine whether prostate cancer is lower risk or higher risk; also called genomic testing, tumor profiling, or molecular tumor testing.
Relationships:
  - Source: BIOPSY
  - Target: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Description: Molecular biomarker testing uses a sample from a biopsy to examine its molecular components.
  - Source: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Target: TREATMENT
  - Description: Biomarker testing results indicate whether treatment should be avoided or delayed.
  - Source: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Target: SURGERY
  - Description: If molecular biomarker testing indicates lower-risk cancer, surgery may be avoided or delayed.
  - Source: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: The care team considers biomarker testing results when assessing risk.
  - Source: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Target: RADIATION THERAPY
  - Description: If molecular biomarker testing indicates lower-risk cancer, radiation therapy may be avoided or delayed.
  - Source: MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Target: PATIENT
  - Description: The patient may have biomarker testing to determine prostate cancer risk.</data>
