    <node id="SURGICAL MENOPAUSE">
      <data key="d3">15</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">SURGICAL MENOPAUSE is menopause caused by surgery, specifically the sudden drop in estrogen that follows the removal of both ovaries. Unlike natural menopause, which occurs gradually, surgical menopause triggers abrupt and often severe symptoms. It is frequently referenced as a comparison point when describing the symptoms of radiation-induced menopause, as both involve an induced cessation of ovarian function.
Relationships:
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: RADIATION-INDUCED MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Radiation-induced menopause has symptoms similar to those caused by surgical menopause.
  - Source: PREMATURE MENOPAUSE
  - Target: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Premature menopause has symptoms similar to surgical menopause.
  - Source: OVARY PRESERVATION
  - Target: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Preserving the ovaries during hysterectomy prevents surgical menopause from removal of both ovaries
  - Source: MENOPAUSE
  - Target: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Menopause is the natural biological transition marking the end of a woman's reproductive years; however, not all menopause occurs naturally. Surgical menopause is a distinct form of menopause caused by surgery. As the descriptions indicate, surgical menopause is a type of menopause that arises specifically as a result of a surgical procedure, rather than through the body's natural hormonal decline. Thus, within the broader category of menopause, surgical menopause is defined by its surgical origin, distinguishing it from spontaneous or naturally occurring menopause. Both descriptions provided are consistent, with no contradictions to resolve: surgical menopause is simply menopause that is induced by surgery. Therefore, it is recognized as a valid and specific subtype of menopause, unified under the same overarching biological condition but differing in its cause.
  - Source: HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Surgical menopause can be caused by hysterectomy that removes the ovaries
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: NIGHT SWEATS
  - Description: Night sweats are a symptom of surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: VAGINAL ATROPHY
  - Description: Vaginal atrophy is a common symptom of surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: BONE LOSS
  - Description: Bone loss is a long-term risk of surgical menopause due to lack of estrogen
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: OSTEOPOROSIS
  - Description: Osteoporosis is a long-term risk of surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: SUDDEN DROP IN ESTROGEN
  - Description: A sudden drop in estrogen causes surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: HOT FLASHES
  - Description: Hot flashes are a symptom of surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: SLEEPING PROBLEMS
  - Description: Sleeping problems are a symptom of surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: WEIGHT GAIN
  - Description: Weight gain is a symptom of surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: CHANGES IN MOOD
  - Description: Changes in mood are a symptom of surgical menopause
  - Source: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Target: CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE
  - Description: Cardiovascular disease is a long-term risk of surgical menopause due to lack of estrogen</data>
