    <node id="BETOBACCOFREE.GOV">
      <data key="d3">8</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">BeTobaccoFree.gov is an online, tobacco-cessation support resource specifically recommended in the provided text to help individuals quit tobacco use. It serves as a comprehensive support website for people seeking to stop smoking, vaping, or using tobacco in any form. The resource is positioned as a reliable quit-smoking aid that offers guidance and support to those who want to overcome nicotine dependence. It is recommended as a support website for quitting tobacco, and is also highlighted as an online resource for finding help with tobacco cessation. Additionally, it is described as a support tool for people who smoke or vape, providing access to assistance for quitting. Overall, BeTobaccoFree.gov functions as a recommended, accessible online destination for anyone looking for help to end their tobacco or vaping habits.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: SMOKING
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov is a tobacco cessation resource related to smoking.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov is listed as an online support resource to help people quit smoking.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: VAPING
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov is also recommended as support for people who vape.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Description: Both are recommended online smoking/vaping cessation support resources.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov and CDC.gov/tobacco are both online support websites designed to help individuals quit smoking or vaping. They are recommended smoking cessation support resources and are frequently listed together in guidance as trusted online options for quitting tobacco use. Both websites serve as accessible, evidence-based quit-smoking and quit-vaping support tools, often cited side by side for individuals seeking help with nicotine addiction.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CANCER TREATMENT
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov is an online resource to help quit tobacco use, which improves cancer treatment outcomes.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, the CDC provides these resources through its dedicated website, CDC.gov/tobacco. Together, BeTobaccoFree.gov and the CDC serve as accessible online support options to help people quit smoking or vaping. Both entities are listed as credible sources of assistance for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and resources for those looking to stop using tobacco products.
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and BeTobaccoFree.gov are two online support websites that are listed together as recommended resources for individuals seeking help to quit smoking, tobacco use, and vaping. Both are highlighted as trusted digital cessation support options, offering guidance and tools for those ready to stop using tobacco products or e-cigarettes.

---</data>
