    <node id="CDC.GOV/TOBACCO">
      <data key="d3">8</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">CDC.GOV/TOBACCO is the official tobacco-related online resource of the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC). It serves as a comprehensive tobacco cessation website, specifically designed to help individuals quit smoking and access a wide range of tobacco-related resources. Recommended as a reliable online support tool, the site provides guidance for those looking to stop smoking or vaping. It is frequently cited as a quit-smoking resource and a valuable source of information for tobacco prevention and cessation.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: SMOKING
  - Description: CDC.gov/tobacco provides information about smoking and tobacco use.
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Description: CDC.gov/tobacco is listed as an online support resource to help people quit smoking.
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: VAPING
  - Description: CDC.gov/tobacco is also recommended as support for people who vape.
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Description: Both are recommended online smoking/vaping cessation support resources.
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: CDC.gov/tobacco is the official tobacco resource page of the CDC (Centers for Disease Control and Prevention). As a dedicated web resource maintained by the CDC, it is designed to provide reliable information and online support for individuals looking to quit smoking or vaping. The CDC is the organization responsible for and associated with this website, ensuring that the content and resources offered align with public health guidelines and evidence-based cessation strategies.
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and CDC.gov/tobacco are both recognized as recommended online resources for quitting smoking and vaping. They are frequently listed together as credible, web-based smoking cessation support options, providing individuals with accessible tools and information to help them stop using tobacco products or e-cigarettes. Both websites serve as authoritative sources of guidance for those seeking to quit.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov and CDC.gov/tobacco are both online support websites designed to help individuals quit smoking or vaping. They are recommended smoking cessation support resources and are frequently listed together in guidance as trusted online options for quitting tobacco use. Both websites serve as accessible, evidence-based quit-smoking and quit-vaping support tools, often cited side by side for individuals seeking help with nicotine addiction.
  - Source: CDC
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) operates the online resource CDC.gov/tobacco, which serves as the agency's dedicated digital platform for tobacco cessation. As the CDC's official online tobacco cessation resource, CDC.gov/tobacco provides information and support to help individuals quit tobacco use, reflecting the CDC's broader public health mission to reduce tobacco-related disease and death. This platform is a key component of the CDC's efforts to offer accessible cessation guidance and resources to the public.

---</data>
