    <node id="MAMMOGRAM">
      <data key="d3">7</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">MAMMOGRAM is an imaging test that produces an x-ray picture of the inside of the breast using low-dose x-rays. It may be performed as a standard 2D digital mammogram or as a 3D mammogram, known as tomosynthesis. The mammogram is used both for breast cancer screening and for the evaluation or diagnosis of breast conditions. It is interpreted by a breast diagnostic radiologist. In addition to screening and diagnosis, a mammogram can also be used to guide a biopsy; when used in this way, the procedure is called a stereotactic needle biopsy.
Relationships:
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: IMAGING
  - Description: Mammogram is a type of imaging test.
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: A mammogram can be used to guide a biopsy.</data>
