    <node id="MENOPAUSE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">(No description provided in the data)
Relationships:
  - Source: MENOPAUSE
  - Target: SURGICAL MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Menopause is the natural biological transition marking the end of a woman's reproductive years; however, not all menopause occurs naturally. Surgical menopause is a distinct form of menopause caused by surgery. As the descriptions indicate, surgical menopause is a type of menopause that arises specifically as a result of a surgical procedure, rather than through the body's natural hormonal decline. Thus, within the broader category of menopause, surgical menopause is defined by its surgical origin, distinguishing it from spontaneous or naturally occurring menopause. Both descriptions provided are consistent, with no contradictions to resolve: surgical menopause is simply menopause that is induced by surgery. Therefore, it is recognized as a valid and specific subtype of menopause, unified under the same overarching biological condition but differing in its cause.
  - Source: MENOPAUSE
  - Target: RADIATION-INDUCED MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Radiation-induced menopause is a form of menopause.
  - Source: MENOPAUSE
  - Target: PREMATURE MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Premature menopause is early menopause.
  - Source: OVARY PRESERVATION
  - Target: MENOPAUSE
  - Description: Preserving the ovaries prevents the sudden drop in estrogen that would cause menopause</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
