      <data key="d1">FIBEROPTIC LARYNGOSCOPY, also known as nasolaryngoscopy, is a diagnostic procedure that uses a small, flexible scope passed through the nose and into the throat. Before the procedure, numbing medicine is sprayed into the nose to minimize discomfort. The procedure itself is quick, typically taking less than one minute to perform.
