      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Panendoscopy uses different types of endoscopes passed down the mouth or nose to perform laryngoscopy, pharyngoscopy, esophagoscopy, or bronchoscopy; it allows a thorough examination of the mouth, oropharynx, larynx, esophagus, trachea, and bronchi, and is performed under anesthesia. Biopsies of abnormal areas may be taken through the scopes.
