    <node id="TREATMENT TRIAL">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A treatment trial is a type of cancer clinical trial that focuses specifically on treatment approaches. Such trials are conducted in phases, which are sequential steps designed to evaluate various aspects of the treatment being studied, including safety, effectiveness, dosing, and comparison with standard therapies. The entity is referred to as "TREATMENT TRIAL."
Relationships:
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: TREATMENT TRIAL
  - Description: Clinical trials are research studies that evaluate medical interventions in human participants. Treatment trials are a specific type of clinical trial, meaning that all treatment trials fall under the broader category of clinical trials. In the context of cancer, treatment trials focus specifically on cancer treatments—testing new therapies, drug combinations, surgical techniques, or other interventions to determine their safety and effectiveness. Because most cancer clinical trials are treatment trials, treatment trials constitute a major subset of clinical research in oncology. Thus, while every treatment trial is a clinical trial, not every clinical trial is a treatment trial; clinical trials also include prevention, screening, diagnostic, and quality-of-life studies. In summary, treatment trials are a type of clinical trial that centers on cancer treatments and represents the majority of cancer-related clinical research.
  - Source: TREATMENT TRIAL
  - Target: PHASE 1 CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Description: Treatment trials are done in phases, including Phase 1 trials.
  - Source: TREATMENT TRIAL
  - Target: PHASE 1 TRIAL
  - Description: Treatment trials are done in phases; Phase 1 trials study dose, safety, and side effects.
  - Source: TREATMENT TRIAL
  - Target: PHASE 2
  - Description: Treatment trials are done in phases; Phase 2 follows Phase 1 in the described sequence.
  - Source: PHASE 3 CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: TREATMENT TRIAL
  - Description: Treatment trials are done in phases, including Phase 3 trials.
  - Source: PHASE 4 CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: TREATMENT TRIAL
  - Description: Treatment trials are done in phases, including Phase 4 trials.
  - Source: PHASE 2 CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: TREATMENT TRIAL
  - Description: Treatment trials are done in phases, including Phase 2 trials.

---</data>
