    <node id="PHASE 2 TRIALS">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Phase 2 trials, also known as Phase 2 clinical trials, are a phase of clinical research that focuses on evaluating how well a drug or treatment approach works against a specific type of cancer. These trials are designed to assess the effectiveness of the intervention in a particular patient population, providing critical data on whether the treatment produces the desired effect. In summary, Phase 2 trials are clinical trials that study the efficacy of a drug or therapeutic approach against a defined cancer type.
Relationships: (None listed in the data.)

