    <node id="DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A diagnostic mammogram is an X-ray imaging test of the breast that takes detailed pictures of both breasts to detect abnormalities, such as cancer or other changes. It is distinct from a screening mammogram, which is used for routine detection in people without symptoms. A diagnostic mammogram is specifically used for individuals who have symptoms such as a lump, breast pain, or nipple changes, or to take a closer look at an abnormal area that was found on a screening mammogram. During this procedure, a radiologist evaluates the images immediately, allowing for prompt assessment of the findings. This test serves as a follow-up and diagnostic tool to clarify whether a suspicious area is benign or requires further investigation.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)</data>
