    <node id="MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Multidisciplinary care is a coordinated healthcare approach in which doctors, specialists, and allied health providers work and communicate as a single, cohesive team. This collaborative model is centered on planning and delivering a patient’s diagnosis and treatment, with the overarching goal of helping the patient through integrated, team-based care. Rather than operating in silos, the various professionals share information and coordinate their efforts to ensure that all aspects of a patient’s condition are addressed comprehensively. By bringing together diverse clinical expertise, multidisciplinary care aims to improve the quality, safety, and effectiveness of patient management, ensuring that diagnostic and therapeutic decisions are made collectively and tailored to the individual’s needs.
Relationships: (None listed in the data)</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">ENTITY: MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE
Description: Multidisciplinary care is a coordinated healthcare approach in which doctors, specialists, and allied health providers work and communicate as a single, cohesive team. This collaborative model is centered on planning and delivering a patient’s diagnosis and treatment, with the overarching goal of helping the patient through integrated, team-based care. Rather than operating in silos, the various professionals share information and coordinate their efforts to ensure that all aspects of a patient’s condition are addressed comprehensively. By bringing together diverse clinical expertise, multidisciplinary care aims to improve the quality, safety, and effectiveness of patient management, ensuring that diagnostic and therapeutic decisions are made collectively and tailored to the individual’s needs.
Relationships: (None listed in the data)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SURGEON">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">SURGEON is a medical professional who specializes in performing surgical procedures. As a physician, the surgeon may also provide cancer genetics counseling and perform diagnostic procedures such as skin biopsies. In the context of cancer care, the surgeon is skilled in identifying and locating sentinel lymph nodes, which are key to determining whether cancer has spread. Thus, the surgeon’s role combines operative expertise with diagnostic and counseling responsibilities in patient care.
Relationships: None listed in the data.</data>
