    <node id="THROAT CANCER">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Throat cancer is a general term used to describe a group of cancers that affect the throat and nearby structures. It encompasses several distinct types, including oropharyngeal cancer, laryngeal cancer, hypopharyngeal cancer, esophageal cancer, and nasopharyngeal cancer. As a category, throat cancer is classified as a head and neck cancer. One notable subtype, oropharyngeal cancer, is most often related to human papillomavirus (HPV) infection. Throat cancer is also the subject of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Throat Cancer, which provide patient-focused information on diagnosis, treatment, and supportive care. Overall, throat cancer represents a diverse set of malignancies with varying risk factors, presentations, and treatment approaches, unified by their location in the throat region.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: LARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: Laryngeal cancer affects the voice box in the throat, so it is a type of throat cancer
  - Source: THROAT CANCER
  - Target: HYPOPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Description: Hypopharyngeal cancer affects the lower part of the throat, so it is a type of throat cancer
  - Source: THROAT CANCER
  - Target: HEAD AND NECK CANCER
  - Description: Throat cancer is a type of head and neck cancer.
  - Source: HEAD AND NECK CANCER
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: Throat cancer is included in the group of cancers arising in the head and neck area
  - Source: NASOPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: Nasopharyngeal cancer affects the nasopharynx, an upper part of the throat, so it is a type of throat cancer
  - Source: ESOPHAGEAL CANCER
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: The text lists esophageal cancer among other types of cancer that affect the throat
  - Source: OROPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: Oropharyngeal cancer is cancer of the middle part of the throat, so it is a type of throat cancer
  - Source: NCCN
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is a direct and authoritative educational resource for patients affected by throat cancer. Specifically, NCCN provides patient guidelines focused on throat cancer, including oropharyngeal cancer, and also offers information on other types of throat cancers. This relationship is defined by NCCN's active publication of patient-oriented guidelines, which serve as a reliable source of education and guidance for individuals seeking information on this disease. These guidelines reflect NCCN's commitment to translating complex clinical knowledge into accessible advice for patients, covering both general throat cancer topics and more specific forms such as oropharyngeal cancer. Through these publications, NCCN directly supports patients in understanding their diagnosis, treatment options, and overall care journey.
  - Source: HPV INFECTION
  - Target: THROAT CANCER
  - Description: Throat cancer is most often related to HPV infection.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
