    <node id="METASTATIC BREAST CANCER">
      <data key="d3">3</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Metastatic breast cancer is advanced breast cancer, as covered in the NCCN patient guideline. It is defined as breast cancer that has spread beyond the breast and the lymph nodes under the arm (axillary lymph nodes). This condition may be categorized as local/regional disease or distant metastasis, depending on the extent and location of the spread.
Relationships:
  - Source: METASTASIS
  - Target: METASTATIC BREAST CANCER
  - Description: Metastatic breast cancer results when breast cancer cells spread through metastasis to distant sites in the body.
  - Source: BREAST CANCER
  - Target: METASTATIC BREAST CANCER
  - Description: Metastatic breast cancer is advanced breast cancer that has spread beyond the breast and nearby lymph nodes. It is a form of breast cancer characterized by the movement of cancer cells from the original tumor site to other parts of the body. Breast cancer, in its earlier stages, is typically confined to the breast tissue and possibly nearby lymph nodes; however, when it becomes metastatic, the disease has progressed to a more advanced stage. Thus, metastatic breast cancer represents the most severe form of breast cancer, in which the cancer has escaped the local region and established itself in distant organs or tissues.
  - Source: NCCN
  - Target: METASTATIC BREAST CANCER
  - Description: NCCN provides comprehensive resources for patients and caregivers about metastatic breast cancer. Specifically, NCCN publishes the patient guideline titled "Breast Cancer – Metastatic," which offers detailed information on this condition. This guideline is accessible through NCCN's official patient resources, including the NCCN.org/patientguidelines website and the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer mobile app. These materials are designed to help individuals understand metastatic breast cancer, its management, and related care considerations. NCCN thus serves as a key source of patient-focused education and support for those affected by metastatic breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
