    <node id="RELATIONSHIP: NCCN -&gt; THROAT CANCER">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is a direct and authoritative educational resource for patients affected by throat cancer. Specifically, NCCN provides patient guidelines focused on throat cancer, including oropharyngeal cancer, and also offers information on other types of throat cancers. This relationship is defined by NCCN's active publication of patient-oriented guidelines, which serve as a reliable source of education and guidance for individuals seeking information on this disease. These guidelines reflect NCCN's commitment to translating complex clinical knowledge into accessible advice for patients, covering both general throat cancer topics and more specific forms such as oropharyngeal cancer. Through these publications, NCCN directly supports patients in understanding their diagnosis, treatment options, and overall care journey.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">ENTITY: RELATIONSHIP: NCCN -&gt; THROAT CANCER
