    <node id="INDUCTION">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Induction is the first phase of treatment for primary CNS lymphoma, lasting several months and typically involving multiple courses of chemotherapy; its goal is to eliminate as many lymphoma cells as possible.
Relationships:
  - Source: INDUCTION
  - Target: TREATMENT FOR THE SPINE
  - Description: If cancer is found in the spine or spinal fluid, a different induction therapy may be recommended, linking treatment for the spine to the induction phase.
  - Source: INDUCTION
  - Target: CONSOLIDATION
  - Description: Induction is the first phase and consolidation is the second phase of treatment; consolidation follows induction and aims to destroy remaining cancer cells.
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: INDUCTION
  - Description: Clinical trial is one of the induction treatment options discussed for primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
