    <node id="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION">
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Digital rectal examination (DRE) is a physical exam event used in the follow-up care of patients who have received chemoradiation. It is recommended as an initial follow-up examination 8 to 12 weeks after completing chemoradiation, specifically to check the results of the treatment. Beyond this early assessment, the DRE also plays a role in longer-term surveillance: it is typically performed every 3 to 6 months for 5 years after treatment. Thus, the digital rectal examination serves both as a short-term response evaluation and as a routine monitoring tool during post-treatment surveillance.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
