    <node id="OPEN BIOPSY">
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Open biopsy is a surgical biopsy procedure in which a neurosurgeon performs a craniotomy, opening the scalp and skull to remove pieces of tumor tissue. It is one of the two standard types of biopsies used for gliomas, and it serves as a surgical procedure to excise a tumor in order to confirm its histology.
Relationships: (No specific relationships listed in the provided data)</data>
