    <node id="STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY">
      <data key="d3">3</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY is a minimally invasive procedure used to diagnose brain conditions, particularly gliomas. It employs a stereotactic frame or tiny skin markers alongside a computerized navigation system that is linked to MRI or CT imaging. This technology precisely guides a thin needle into the brain to extract a small sliver or sample of tumor tissue. The technique is especially valuable for lesions that are hard to reach or located in vital brain areas, as it allows accurate sampling with minimal damage to surrounding healthy tissue.
Relationships: None listed</data>
