    <node id="BONE MARROW BIOPSY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone marrow biopsy is a diagnostic procedure that involves the removal of a sample of bone marrow tissue for testing. It is typically performed as a bedside procedure using a wider needle to extract a core sample of bone marrow. The sample is often taken from the back of the hip bone. This procedure may cause temporary bone pain and bruising. A bone marrow biopsy is frequently performed at the same time as a bone marrow aspirate. It is used to confirm a diagnosis of acute myeloid leukemia (AML) and to evaluate bone marrow health for various other conditions.
Relationships: (No specific relationships listed in the provided data)</data>
