    <node id="CORE BIOPSY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Core biopsy (CB) is a medical procedure and a specific type of biopsy. It involves the use of a needle—typically a hollow needle—to remove a sample of tissue or fluid from the body. In particular, core biopsy is commonly employed to obtain tissue samples from a tumor, allowing for diagnostic examination. The procedure is minimally invasive and is used to gather material for further analysis, such as determining whether a tumor is benign or malignant.
Relationships: (No specific relationships listed in the provided data)</data>
