      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fine-needle aspiration is a biopsy type for suspicious lymph nodes; it is also known simply as needle biopsy [Data: Entities (872)]. Fine-needle biopsy (FNB) is a needle-based biopsy procedure that uses a needle to remove a sample of tissue from a tumor or lymph node. It can be guided by imaging techniques such as ultrasound or computed tomography (CT) to ensure accurate placement of the needle [Data: Entities (540)]. Needle biopsy is a medical procedure in which a needle is used to extract a sample of tissue or fluid from the body for diagnostic testing. It is often performed on a lymph node, allowing pathologists to examine the sample for abnormalities such as infection or cancer [Data: Entities (366)].
</data>
