    <node id="EGG FREEZING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Egg freezing, also known medically as oocyte cryopreservation or oocyte preservation, is a fertility preservation method in which unfertilized eggs are removed from a woman’s ovaries, frozen, and stored for later use. This procedure allows individuals to preserve their reproductive potential by safeguarding eggs for future fertilization attempts, typically when they are not yet ready to conceive or when medical treatments may affect fertility.
Relationships: (No relationships listed in the data)</data>
