    <node id="SEXUAL REPRODUCTION">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Sexual reproduction is a biological process for which the female reproductive system is specialized. In this process, the ovaries produce eggs, which are essential for sexual reproduction. Furthermore, sexual reproduction requires both the eggs made by the ovaries and hormones, which play a key role in enabling the process. Thus, the female reproductive system, egg production, and hormonal regulation are all integral to sexual reproduction.
Relationships: (None listed in the data)

