    <node id="STANDARD SURGICAL EXCISION">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard surgical excision is a conventional surgical procedure used to remove skin cancer, specifically cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC) and squamous cell skin cancer. The procedure involves removing the tumor along with a margin of surrounding healthy skin to ensure complete removal of cancerous tissue. This approach is recommended for treating localized CSCC. In some cases, a skin graft may be performed following the excision to repair the area where the skin was removed.
