**ENTITY: PHASE 4 TRIALS**
Description: Phase 4 trials are a phase of clinical research that study the long-term safety and benefit of an FDA-approved treatment. These trials are conducted after a treatment has already received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration, focusing on monitoring its real-world effectiveness and any potential side effects over an extended period. As clinical trials, Phase 4 trials help gather additional information on how the treatment performs in a broader patient population, ensuring that its benefits continue to outweigh any risks in everyday medical practice.
Relationships: (None listed in the data.)

---

