    <edge source="NCCN" target="BREAST CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides patient guidelines for breast cancer. These guidelines comprehensively cover breast cancer basics, including information on the disease itself, as well as guidance on testing and treatment planning. The NCCN's patient guidelines address the full spectrum of breast cancer, specifically including ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS), invasive breast cancer, and metastatic breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="HEAD AND NECK CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides patient-centered resources for individuals facing head and neck cancers. These offerings include patient guidelines specifically tailored to cancers of the head and neck region, as well as a dedicated Patient Guides for Cancer mobile app that delivers accessible information and guidance. The NCCN's patient information covers a broad range of malignancies in this anatomical area, with explicit inclusion of nasopharyngeal and oropharyngeal cancers, ensuring comprehensive education and support for patients navigating diagnosis, treatment, and survivorship.</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
