    <edge source="NCCN" target="OROPHARYNGEAL CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides patient-focused information on oropharyngeal cancer, commonly referred to as throat cancer. This resource is available through the NCCN Patient Guidelines, accessible online at NCCN.org/patientguidelines. Additionally, the same information can be found in the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app. These materials offer guidance on the condition, including details about diagnosis, treatment, and support, to help patients and their families understand and manage oropharyngeal cancer. NCCN's patient guidelines are designed to be accessible and practical, translating the organization's evidence-based, expert consensus recommendations into plain language for individuals affected by cancer. Through both the website and the mobile app, NCCN ensures that reliable, up-to-date information about oropharyngeal cancer is widely available to patients, caregivers, and the public.</data>
      <data key="d8">OROPHARYNGEAL CANCER</data>
    </edge>
