      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">NCCN publishes patient guidelines and a patient guides app containing information about basal cell skin cancer</data>
      <data key="d8">BASAL CELL SKIN CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="THROAT CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is a direct and authoritative educational resource for patients affected by throat cancer. Specifically, NCCN provides patient guidelines focused on throat cancer, including oropharyngeal cancer, and also offers information on other types of throat cancers. This relationship is defined by NCCN's active publication of patient-oriented guidelines, which serve as a reliable source of education and guidance for individuals seeking information on this disease. These guidelines reflect NCCN's commitment to translating complex clinical knowledge into accessible advice for patients, covering both general throat cancer topics and more specific forms such as oropharyngeal cancer. Through these publications, NCCN directly supports patients in understanding their diagnosis, treatment options, and overall care journey.</data>
      <data key="d8">THROAT CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">NCCN publishes the patient guideline 'Breast Cancer Ductal Carcinoma In Situ'</data>
      <data key="d8">DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="METASTATIC BREAST CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">NCCN provides comprehensive resources for patients and caregivers about metastatic breast cancer. Specifically, NCCN publishes the patient guideline titled "Breast Cancer Metastatic," which offers detailed information on this condition. This guideline is accessible through NCCN's official patient resources, including the NCCN.org/patientguidelines website and the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer mobile app. These materials are designed to help individuals understand metastatic breast cancer, its management, and related care considerations. NCCN thus serves as a key source of patient-focused education and support for those affected by metastatic breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d8">METASTATIC BREAST CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CHEMOTHERAPY" target="TREATMENT TEAM" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The treatment team explains how often, how long, and how chemotherapy is given and its side effects</data>
      <data key="d8">TREATMENT TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CHEMOTHERAPY" target="CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Chemotherapy uses anti-cancer medicines that travel in the bloodstream to reach cells throughout the body, including cancer cells</data>
      <data key="d8">CANCER</data>
    </edge>
