    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="OVARIAN CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The guide describes treatment recommendations for ovarian cancer as a cancer treatment process.</data>
      <data key="d8">OVARIAN CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="BIOPSY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Biopsy results are used to determine cancer stage treatment plan</data>
      <data key="d8">BIOPSY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="FERTILITY PRESERVATION" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Fertility preservation is an important consideration for individuals who are about to begin cancer treatment. It should be considered and planned before starting cancer treatment, as cancer therapies such as chemotherapy, radiation, or surgery may affect fertility. Therefore, fertility preservation should be addressed prior to the initiation of cancer treatment to allow for the best possible options and outcomes. In summary, both consideration and planning for fertility preservation should occur before starting cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d8">FERTILITY PRESERVATION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER TREATMENT" target="DIAGNOSIS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Emotional support is needed during diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d8">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IMAGING" target="PATIENT" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The patient should obtain copies of imaging results and keep them organized.</data>
      <data key="d8">PATIENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IMAGING" target="COLON CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
