    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPPORTIVE CARE" target="MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Multidisciplinary care teams are central to the delivery of supportive care for cancer patients. These teams are responsible for both providing supportive care services directly and for arranging access to such services as needed. In this context, supportive care encompasses the range of physical, emotional, and practical assistance that addresses the broader needs of patients beyond direct cancer treatment. The multidisciplinary care model ensures that supportive care is integrated into the patient's overall care plan, with various professionals collaborating to meet the patient's comprehensive needs. Thus, the relationship between supportive care and multidisciplinary care is one of service delivery, where the team acts as the primary mechanism for ensuring patients receive the supportive care they require.</data>
      <data key="d8">SUPPORTIVE CARE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUITTING SMOKING" target="CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
