      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mouth cancer is a type of head and neck cancer. It belongs to the broader category of head and neck cancers, which includes several distinct cancer types. Thus, mouth cancer is one of the several cancers grouped under the head and neck cancer classification.</data>
      <data key="d8">HEAD AND NECK CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MOUTH CANCER" target="SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is the most common type of mouth cancer. Mouth cancer encompasses various malignancies, and among them, squamous cell carcinoma is the most frequently diagnosed form. Both statements confirm that SCC, also referred to as squamous cell carcinoma, represents the predominant subtype of mouth cancer.</data>
      <data key="d8">SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA</data>
    </edge>
