    <edge source="GENERAL HEALTH TESTS" target="FAMILY HISTORY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">General health tests include family history</data>
      <data key="d8">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GENERAL HEALTH TESTS" target="TOBACCO AND ALCOHOL USE HISTORY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">General health tests include tobacco and alcohol use history</data>
      <data key="d8">TOBACCO AND ALCOHOL USE HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GENERAL HEALTH TESTS" target="MEDICAL HISTORY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">General health tests encompass a range of evaluations used to assess an individual's overall well-being, and they include the medical history as a fundamental component. Specifically, the medical history is recognized as one of the key general health tests, meaning it is an integral part of the initial health assessment process. Beyond simply being a component, the medical history plays a crucial role in guiding clinical decision-making: it helps determine which additional tests and treatments are relevant and appropriate for the individual. In this way, the medical history both serves as a foundational element of general health testing and shapes the subsequent course of care based on the patient's unique background, prior conditions, and risk factors.</data>
      <data key="d8">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GENERAL HEALTH TESTS" target="PHYSICAL EXAM" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">GENERAL HEALTH TESTS encompass a range of routine medical evaluations, and PHYSICAL EXAM is one of the key components included within them. In other words, a physical exam is one of the general health tests performed to assess overall health.</data>
      <data key="d8">PHYSICAL EXAM</data>
    </edge>
