    </edge>
    <edge source="NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK" target="BPDCN" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is a professional organization that develops clinical practice guidelines for cancer care. Among its resources, the NCCN Guidelines for Patients include a dedicated chapter addressing the treatment of BPDCNblastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm, a rare and aggressive blood cancer. This chapter is part of the NCCN's patient-focused educational materials, which are designed to help patients understand their diagnosis and treatment options. The NCCN's coverage of BPDCN in its patient guidelines reflects the organization's commitment to providing up-to-date, evidence-based information for both clinicians and patients. The inclusion of this chapter ensures that individuals affected by BPDCN have accessible guidance on available therapeutic approaches, as outlined by the NCCN's expert panel. Thus, the NCCN directly supports patient education and informed decision-making for BPDCN through this specific chapter in its guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d8">BPDCN</data>
    </edge>
