    <edge source="ECHOCARDIOGRAM" target="ULTRASOUND" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An echocardiogram is a type of ultrasound. Specifically, an echocardiogram is an ultrasound procedure that uses sound waves to create pictures of the heart. In this context, ultrasound refers both to the broader imaging modality and to the technology that employs high-frequency sound waves to visualize internal structures. The echocardiogram, as a specialized application of ultrasound, focuses on the heart, allowing healthcare providers to examine its structure and function in detail. Together, these descriptions establish that the echocardiogram is a subset of ultrasound, distinguished by its use of sound waves to generate images of the heart.</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
    </edge>
